*> Game time of the replica (PL-GAME-TIME): Set Time (0x73) gives the world's game time in its first field, whatever the clock updates say, and each client tick adds 1. The
*> wolf's anger end time (Set Entity Data entry 22) is a game time and is compared with it (34-5 2.5), not with the daylight clock.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-GAME-TIME.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 4096.
 01 WS-CONN                BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG VALUE 115.
 01 WS-ONE                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-TIME                BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 WS-PARTIAL             FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-RATE                FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 1.0.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "NET-BUFFERS-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN
     MOVE PH-PLAY TO CN-PHASE(WS-CONN)
     MOVE 1 TO PL-HAS-SKY
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE 123456 TO WS-TIME
     CALL "PB-PUT-LONG" USING PB-BUFFER WS-TIME
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ONE
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     MOVE 5000 TO WS-TIME
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARLONG" USING PB-BUFFER WS-TIME
     CALL "PB-PUT-FLOAT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-PARTIAL
     CALL "PB-PUT-FLOAT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-RATE
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "PROTO-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN PB-BUFFER WS-ID
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "game time: Set Time keeps its first field as the game time" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 123456 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-GAME-TIME TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "game time: the clock update still sets the daylight clock" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 5000 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-DAY-TICKS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-GAME-TIME.
 COPY CLTEST.
